@startuml ATTEMPTS
' examples/promote/ATTEMPTS.puml with every clause written in Python, read
' through the reference glue. Fee bumping: a stuck attempt is replaced by one
' that pays more. The constrain says what a replacement is; the assume note
' says what no guard can - that the replacements stop.
state "稼働中" as running {
  running : attempts ; 試行ID ⇸ Attempt

  state "attempts : 試行ID ⇸ Attempt" as runningAttempts <<promote>> {
    !include local/ATTEMPT.puml
  }
}

[*] --> running : [{'attempts': FrozenMap()}]
' The scenario may rest once every attempt is confirmed.
running --> [*] : len(attempts) > 0 and all(r.state == '確定' for r in attempts.values())

note bottom of runningAttempts
  constrain RESEND?試行ID?置換Tx ; 置換Tx.置換元 in attempts and attempts[置換Tx.置換元].state == '滞留' and 置換Tx.手数料 > attempts[置換Tx.置換元].手数料
end note

note as fair
  assume 手数料を上げた置換を続ければ、いつかいずれかの試行が〈確定〉になる
end note
@enduml
